  WHAT IS AND IS NOT SUBSTANTIVE HERE, said before the numbers.
  sum_e k_r(e|h) = 1 is an IDENTITY of the construction: G(h, r)
  is defined as sum_e q(e|h) G(h+e, r-1) and k_r divides by it.
  Verifying it is a REGRESSION TRIPWIRE on the extraction and on
  the menu bookkeeping — it catches a menu used in the kernel
  that differs from the menu used in the potential — and it is
  labelled as one.  The three SUBSTANTIVE properness questions
  are gated separately below: (a) strict positivity of every
  potential (a zero denominator is the only way the identity can
  break), (b) non-negativity of every kernel entry, and (c)
  CUT-ADDITIVITY of the chained measure — the transport analogue
  of the d42a defect the pin's HZ-IV names.
