  [PASS] HZ1-b STRICT POSITIVITY AND NON-NEGATIVITY — the substantive half.  Every one of the potentials above is strictly positive (so no kernel is defined by a zero denominator) and every kernel entry is >= 0, so each k_r really is a probability on the menu and not merely a normalized signed weight.  The mechanism is in the committed layer: the idle option is emitted at every history and its weight 1 - (1/4)(has_p) - (1/4)(has_am) - (1/4)(has_d) is at worst 1/4  (non-positive potentials = 0; negative kernel entries = 0, over 279067 kernels)
